"Ultimately, scientific progress and moral responsibility are not rival forces locked in a zero-sum struggle; they are twin pillars of an enlightened civilization. Science provides the indispensable illumination of empirical truth, while ethics supplies the compass that prevents knowledge from degenerating into reckless power. By uniting intellectual daring with moral humility, humanity can ensure that its deepest inquiries serve the dignity of life and the preservation of our shared world."
